    {
      "source_file": "icrs/202405-1218-005/raw/supporting-statement-a-1.txt",
      "preceding_text": "Our lead economist assisted us in the update of this paperwork package in February.\u00a0 They verified that the increase in numbers were driven in part by a jump from 2012 to 2018 data from EIA\u2019s Commercial Buildings Energy Consumption Survey (and to a lesser extend a jump in a parallel Manufacturing Energy Consumption Survey (MECS) from 2010 to 2018).\u00a0 The chart below shows which years data was used for the most recent ICRs at the time of the update. \u00a0\u00a0These types of large studies are not usually conducted annually, and we use the data that is most current at the time the ICR is up for renewal. As you can see in the table the studies have a gap of six years when they update the data.",
